{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Following any vertex’s edges eventually repeats, so each weakly connected component holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly one cycle, with rooted trees hanging off its vertices (Flajolet and Odlyzko, “Random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mapping statistics”, EUROCRYPT ’89). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cycleDecomposition()"},{"type":"text","text":" finds every cycle and tree in O(n);"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successor(of:steps:)"},{"type":"text","text":" answers f^k(v) for any k."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For f given as a closure over a state space too large to store, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"floydCycleDetection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"brentCycleDetection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which need only ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" states and O(1) memory.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" One ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" per vertex, ","type":"text"},{"code":"f(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The edge leaving ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has position ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions and edge indices are both the source. For ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" vertex labels, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LabeledGraph<Label, FunctionalGraph>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"LabeledGraph(FunctionalGraph(g)!, labels: g.vertices)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gives a graph ","type":"text"},{"code":"g","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" its labels back.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph is immutable: build a new one to change f.","type":"text"}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CycleDecomposition"],"anchor":"Structures","generated":true},{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(successors:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(vertexCount:successor:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/cycleDecomposition()","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/successor(of:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/successor(of:steps:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CustomDebugStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Decodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/Func